# Generated by Cargo
# will have compiled files and executables
debug
target

# These are backup files generated by rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk

# MSVC Windows builds of rustc generate these, which store debugging information
*.pdb

# Generated by cargo mutants
# Contains mutation testing data
**/mutants.out*/

# Secrets.
#
# autumn-web loads `.env`, `.env.local`, `.env.{profile}` and
# `.env.{profile}.local` into the config layer, and `BOIDBOARD_HARVEST_ADMIN_TOKEN`
# — the credential that unlocks Harvest's engine-level management API — is read
# from exactly those files. None of them were ignored, so the first person to
# set it locally would have committed it.
#
# `.env.example` is the one that stays tracked: it documents the variable names
# without carrying a value.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# NOT ignored, deliberately: `autumn-dev.toml` is configuration, not a secret —
# it names the local database everyone on the project uses and is meant to be
# committed. `.env*` above is where anything with a real credential goes.

# RustRover
#  JetBrains specific template is maintained in a separate JetBrains.gitignore that can
#  be found at https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Global/JetBrains.gitignore
#  and can be added to the global gitignore or merged into this file.  For a more nuclear
#  option (not recommended) you can uncomment the following to ignore the entire idea folder.
#.idea/
